= The Kurdish Issue

{!<img src="img/kurdish-issue.jpg" alt="Kurdish public meeting" style="display:block;max-width:100%;max-height:320px;margin:12px auto;object-fit:contain">!}

The Kurdish question has been one of the most difficult issues facing our young republic. Armed attempts to break away from Turkey or change its political structure were crushed during Atatürk's presidency. Since then, the region has been pacified, and the Kurdish population largely accepts life within the republic. This does not mean that the situation has resolved itself. Rising radicalism, inadequate government action, and the failure to protect Kurdish citizens from state violence have continued to worsen the situation. Now that we are in power, it is time to fulfil the promises made to Kurdish citizens under CHP's new agenda on the Kurdish Issue.

- @associations: Remove administrative and legal obstacles to Kurdish citizens forming and organizing Kurdish associations.
- @public_discussion: Lift restrictions on discussing the Kurdish Issue in the public sphere.
- @publishing: Grant legal permission for regulated Kurdish printing and publishing activities.
- @meetings: Ease restrictions on the right to hold meetings and demonstrations.
- @oversight: Strengthen protection and oversight against unlawful violence by public officials and security forces.
- @agricultural_efforts: Agricultural efforts
- @back_to_main: Back to main menu.
- @decline: We will not take an action at the moment.

@associations
title: Remove administrative and legal obstacles to Kurdish citizens forming and organizing Kurdish associations.
new-page: true
choose-if: {! return !AnatolianSocialIssues.reason(Q,"associations"); !}
